@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] data-no-user-credentials
The phone talks to one server, the one set in Settings, with no user sign-in: the only
credentials it holds are the optional Cloudflare Access client ID and secret, which are
sent only to that server, stored only on the phone, and never logged or shown back in
full.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] data-server-is-the-source
The phone reads pull requests, diffs, tours and AI work from its server's API, the same
actions the web app runs; it never calls GitHub or a model provider itself.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-lite-diffs
A large pull request opens from a `lite` diff: files past the patch budget arrive with no
hunks and `patchOmitted`, show skeletons where their code goes, and get their hunks from
`diff-patches` (rules 51 and 52; architecture, The phone reads the server's store).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-tours-are-kept
Tours the person has opened are stored on the phone, so they open at once the next time
(CHANGELOG 0.28.0).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-jev-polls-briefly
While Inbox rows lack Jev's read and the Inbox needs it, the phone reads `my-pulls-cached`
with `revalidate: false` and `classify: true` every three seconds for two minutes at most,
and never shows a loading screen for it (architecture, Jev; rule 51).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-file-marks-follow-the-head
The phone drops a diff's file marks when the pull request's head moves, and shows Jev's
read only for the current head and title (architecture, Jev).
